1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,660
Can you roll your tongue?

2
00:00:01,660 --> 00:00:03,251
Try it right now.

3
00:00:03,396 --> 00:00:04,290
Can't?

4
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:05,933
Don't blame your parents.

5
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:08,030
Your tongue has no bones.

6
00:00:08,030 --> 00:00:09,290
It's all muscle...

7
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:10,967
like an octopus arm.

8
00:00:11,023 --> 00:00:12,254
Rolling means curling

9
00:00:12,254 --> 00:00:13,357
both edges up

10
00:00:13,357 --> 00:00:14,733
at ONCE.

11
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:15,477
School books say

12
00:00:15,477 --> 00:00:17,333
you get that from your parents.

13
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:19,160
But identical twins?

14
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:20,458
Same genes...

15
00:00:20,458 --> 00:00:21,557
one could,

16
00:00:21,557 --> 00:00:22,567
one couldn't.

17
00:00:22,623 --> 00:00:23,850
The scientist behind it

18
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:25,233
said he was embarrassed.

19
00:00:25,261 --> 00:00:26,563
And kids have emailed

20
00:00:26,563 --> 00:00:27,715
a scientist asking

21
00:00:27,715 --> 00:00:29,600
if they're ADOPTED.

22
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:30,467
They're not.

23
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:31,748
Try again.

